        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0be008ed-829f-55b4-ac41-b8ee3788236b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jon Heder, Rob Schneider, David Spade, Patrick Stewart, James Roday, Julianna Guill, Cheryl Hines, Gary Cole, Roy Disney\n- Films and TV: Napoleon Dynamite, The Benchwarmers, School for Scoundrels, Blades of Glory, Mama's Boy, When in Rome, Walt Before Mickey, Monster House, Surf's Up, Christmas Eve, Agent Cody Banks, Skyrunners, Veronica Mars, 10 Things I Hate About You, You Wish!\n- Companies: Revolution Studios, Happy Madison Productions, Columbia Pictures\n- Music: Junk, Ritalin, Life Is Good\n- Roles: actor, producer, voice actor\n\nFacts:\n- Jon Heder was born on October 26, 1977, and he is an American actor and producer.\n- Jon Heder made his feature film debut in 2004 as the title character in the comedy film Napoleon Dynamite.\n- Jon Heder later acted in The Benchwarmers, School for Scoundrels, Blades of Glory, Mama's Boy, When in Rome, and Walt Before Mickey, in which he portrayed Roy Disney.\n- Jon Heder also provided voice acting in the animated films Monster House and Surf's Up and in the Napoleon Dynamite animated series.\n- The Benchwarmers stars Rob Schneider, David Spade, and Jon Heder.\n- The Benchwarmers was produced by Revolution Studios and Happy Madison Productions and distributed by Columbia Pictures.\n- The 2015 film Christmas Eve features an ensemble cast led by Patrick Stewart, James Roday, Julianna Guill, Jon Heder, Cheryl Hines, and Gary Cole.\n- Junk's song Life Is Good was first recorded in the U.S. when the band was called Ritalin, and the song appeared in films and television shows including Agent Cody Banks, The Benchwarmers, Skyrunners, Veronica Mars, 10 Things I Hate About You, and You Wish!",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
